The attached image illustrates the active transport of Nano-11 nanoparticles to the draining lymph nodes by antigen-presenting cells (APCs). Figure 4a shows flow cytometry plots where Nano-11-containing myeloid cells in the lymph node peaked at 3.5% on day 2 post-injection, decreasing to 0.5% by day 7. Figure 4c reveals that Nano-11 is predominantly found in migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) over time. Figure 4d further highlights that MigDCs exhibited significantly higher mean fluorescence intensity (MFI), indicating more efficient Nano-11 uptake per cell compared to lymphoid tissue resident DCs (LTDCs) and monocytes/macrophages (Mo/MΦ), supporting Nano-11's effective targeting to key immune cells.